faq:
  - q: What is student counselling?
    a: Student counselling is a specialised psychological support service for university students covering academic stress, adjustment difficulties, identity, loneliness and anxiety.
  - q: Why should university students seek therapy?
    a: Living alone in a new city, academic pressure, identity exploration and relationship issues can all affect mental health. Early support strengthens both academic performance and personal growth.
  - q: Is counselling available in English in Famagusta?
    a: Yes. Our team provides sessions in both Turkish and English, making our services accessible to international students at universities in North Cyprus.
  - q: Is student counselling confidential?
    a: Yes. Sessions and your personal information are protected in line with our confidentiality principles. What you discuss is not shared with your university, your department, a scholarship body or your family.
  - q: How many sessions does student counselling take?
    a: There is no set number. With some individuals we work on a single subject over a few sessions; with others we continue regularly through the semester. We decide on frequency and length together.
